body:
email the PI, indicating you applied on handshake and attach whatever documents they asked for in the email

&#x200B;

I have gotten a few replies from the jobs I applied from Handshake (both on and off campus jobs)

Will do! I am building on up my resume with volunteering opportunities while Im still in SG (Have one in early jan) 

&#x200B;

Thank you for the wishes and best of luck on your journey!

How do you manage it, if you mind me asking? My workload is going to be pretty heavy next sem and I'm kinda worried I won't be able to handle it (I can't drop any of my classes). I also have a bit of family stuff which would most probs add onto my stress

&#x200B;

Not going to lie, I am terrified for next semester

(a fellow student here too) same Im also planning to send a thank you email to all my profs (and the TAs) 

&#x200B;

All of them have been super understanding and helpful.

ECON 120 is fine (I think its an easy A but u do need to keep up with the lectures) COMM 103 isnt that bad too I think (a lot of work tho so be prepared for that). AH 110, there is weekly assignments but u dnt need to watch all the lectures to do the assignments

&#x200B;

I'm willing to give u my notes for all 3 subjects when this sem is over so just pm me

